    "narrative": "For today's matchup, the highest offensive ceiling lies with **Daulton Varsho** (69.94) and **Taylor Ward** (67.66). **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Quantrill (xERA 4.81) and a notable SB opportunity against a slow delivery, while **Taylor Ward** leverages a massive 16% park boost to offset a tough individual matchup against Griffin. **Luis Arraez** (66.05) and **Tyler Freeman** (66.17) round out our top-tier plays; **Luis Arraez** is locked into a projected leadoff spot with wind-aided potential, and **Tyler Freeman** enjoys the cleanest matchup of the day against Paredes, who carries a shaky 5.42 xERA.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Geraldo Perdomo**, who finished at 47.91, narrowly missing the cut behind **Jeremiah Jackson**. While **Geraldo Perdomo** offers strong leadoff-order upside, his raw efficiency against Sulser was suppressed by negative park factors and a difficult SP matchup, forcing the optimizer to favor the higher, albeit volatile, output potential of the rest of the starting nine. We are also closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert** against Bryce Elder. While the wind-out conditions at the stadium provide a collective lift for this group, any shifts in the batting order, particularly for **Drew Gilbert** at the bottom of the order, could force an immediate re-evaluation of his 51.56 score. \n\nFinally, a note on positional depth: while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains on the IL, we continue to stash high-upside assets like **Gavin Sheets**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Will Smith**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Ryan Waldschmidt** for future flexibility. Today\u2019s lineup prioritizes the current efficiency scores provided by Steamer, leaning heavily on the SB-conducive profiles of **Masyn Winn**, **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Daulton Varsho** to maintain our competitive edge in our scarcest category.",
